{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5436) from the cobbler orchestrator pipeline. The task is to implement srd063-timeout requirements R4.1-R4.4, which are the **differential testing** requirements for `cmd/timeout`. Specifically:\n   - R4.1: Differential tests must compare exit codes between Go binary and reference binary (`gtimeout`) via `pkg/testutils`\n   - R4.2: Tests must cover: command completes before timeout, command exceeds timeout (exit 124), duration 0, `-s` with named/numeric signals, `-k` kill-after escalation, `--preserve-status`, and error cases (no args, invalid duration, command not found)\n   - R4.3: Tests must use fast commands (`true`, `false`, `sleep 0`) and short durations to avoid slow test execution\n   - R4.4: Tests must verify that the timed-out process is actually killed and does not remain as an orphan\n\n   Acceptance criteria require: `go build` succeeds, `go vet` clean, `go test` passes, all four R4 requirements implemented, existing tests continue to pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gtimeout`) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Process group management via `SysProcAttr.Setpgid` for signal delivery to child process groups\n   - Signal handling (SIGTERM, SIGKILL, SIGHUP, etc.) and exit code conventions (124 for timeout, 125 for internal error, 126/127 for exec failure, 128+signum for signal death)\n   - Duration parsing with suffix multipliers (s, m, h, d) and fractional values\n   - Kill-after escalation: send initial signal, then SIGKILL after additional duration\n   - `--preserve-status` flag: exit with command's signal-death status instead of 124\n   - `--foreground` flag: don't create separate process group\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `testutils.NormalizeFunc` for clearing stderr differences between implementations\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd063-timeout.yaml**\n     - The SRD specification defining all requirements for cmd/timeout\n     - R4 group (lines 54-64) defines the differential testing requirements being implemented\n     - Non-goals clarify: no --verbose, no platform-specific process group management beyond SysProcAttr.Setpgid\n   \n   - **cmd/timeout/main.go** (361 lines, existing, to be modified)\n     - Complete implementation from R1-R3 groups already exists\n     - Key structures: `options` struct (signal, killAfter, foreground, preserveStatus, duration, cmdArgs)\n     - Key functions: `main()`, `runWithTimeout()`, `exitCode()`, `sendSignal()`, `reraiseSignal()`, `parseArgs()`, `parseLongFlag()`, `parseShortFlags()`, `parseDuration()`, `parseSignal()`\n     - Uses `time.AfterFunc` for timeout and kill-after timers\n     - Process group kill via `syscall.Kill(-cmd.Process.Pid, sig)` in non-foreground mode\n     - Signal map covers all standard Unix signals\n     - May need minor modifications for R4.4 (orphan process prevention)\n   \n   - **cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go** (179 lines, existing, to be modified)\n     - Already has differential testing setup with `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gtimeout\")`\n     - Has `clearStderr` normalizer: `func(b []byte) []byte { return nil }`\n     - Already has 26 test cases covering most of R4.2's required scenarios\n     - Tests use `ExitCode: -1` for cases where exit code varies (signal-killed processes)\n     - **Missing**: R4.4 test for verifying timed-out process is actually killed (orphan check)\n     - May need additional test cases to fully satisfy R4.1-R4.4\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reading was completed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read all three required files (SRD, main.go, test file) to understand current state\n   - Identified that the existing test file already covers most of R4.2's scenarios\n   - Key gap identified: R4.4 requires a test verifying the timed-out process is actually killed and doesn't remain as an orphan - this is not yet covered\n   - Need to determine if main.go needs any changes or if this is purely a test task\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The first user message is the massive task prompt containing all project context, SRDs, architecture, task description, constraints, and execution constitution for implementing srd063-timeout R4.1-R4.4\n   - The second user message is: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" requesting a summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R4.1-R4.4 requirements (differential testing for cmd/timeout)\n   - Specifically need to add R4.4 orphan-process-verification test\n   - Review if any additional test cases are needed for complete R4.2 coverage\n   - Possibly modify main.go if any changes are needed to support testability\n   - Run `go build -o bin/timeout ./cmd/timeout/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/timeout/...` for lint checks\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/timeout/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three files needed for the task:\n   1. `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd063-timeout.yaml` - the SRD with R4 requirements\n   2. `cmd/timeout/main.go` - the existing 361-line implementation\n   3. `cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go` - the existing 179-line test file with 26 test cases\n\n   I was about to begin the implementation phase. The existing test file already has good coverage for R4.1-R4.3 (differential testing structure, scenario coverage, fast commands). The main gap is R4.4 which requires verifying the timed-out process is actually killed and doesn't remain as an orphan. This likely requires a test that:\n   - Starts a command via timeout with a short duration\n   - Waits for the timeout to occur\n   - Checks that the child process PID no longer exists\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the remaining R4.4 test case(s) in `cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go` to verify orphan process cleanup, and review existing tests for any R4.2 coverage gaps. Then run `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` to verify all acceptance criteria pass. The task description states: \"Tests must verify that the timed-out process is actually killed and does not remain as an orphan\" (R4.4). The existing 26 test cases need to be augmented with at least one test that explicitly checks process termination. Since the task says \"Do NOT modify files outside the Files to Create/Modify list\", changes are limited to `cmd/timeout/main.go` and `cmd/timeout/timeout_test.go`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5436/95fe952a-2927-4d0c-af53-a51330592c95.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95fe952a-2927-4d0c-af53-a51330592c95","uuid":"c900d325-00a9-4583-a171-c806c80e3bd6","timestamp":"2026-05-21T18:40:40.603Z","isSynthetic":true}
